{"the_cosine_similarity_between_each_matched_q_x_and_k_m": "The object \"the cosine similarity between each matched _q_ ( _**x**_ ) and _**k**_ _m_\" refers to the measure of similarity between the input-conditioned query produced by the pretrained ViT encoder and the selected key from the pool of learnable keys. This similarity is quantified using the cosine similarity metric."},
{"the_approach": "The approach refers to the method used by L2P and DualPrompt for selecting prompts from a pool using an image-wise prompt query. This involves a key-value pair based query strategy to dynamically choose instance-specific prompts.|Here is another description: The approach refers to the method used by L2P and DualPrompt for selecting prompts from a pool using an image-wise prompt query, which involves a key-value pair based query strategy."},
