{"mitigating_catastrophic_forgetting__requires__avoidance_of_overwriting_knowledge_acquired_in_prior_tasks": "Requires indicates a necessary condition or prerequisite. In the context of mitigating catastrophic forgetting, it signifies that a specific action or strategy is essential to achieve the desired outcome of preserving prior knowledge during new learning tasks."},
{"avoidance_of_overwriting_knowledge_acquired_in_prior_tasks": "Avoidance of overwriting knowledge acquired in prior tasks means implementing measures to ensure that new information does not erase or significantly alter previously learned data. This involves strategies such as freezing existing parameters and only updating new components when learning new tasks."},
{"new_task": "The new task refers to a fresh learning objective introduced in a sequence of tasks designed to mitigate catastrophic forgetting. It represents a distinct challenge or goal that the system aims to achieve without losing previously acquired knowledge."},
{"new_task__involves__freezing_current_components_and_expanding_the_set": "The predicate \"involves\" signifies the necessary actions or steps that are part of addressing the new task. In this context, it highlights the specific strategy employed to handle the new task while preserving existing knowledge."},
{"freezing_current_components_and_expanding_the_set": "Freezing current components and expanding the set is a strategy used to prevent overwriting of previously learned knowledge. It involves locking the existing parameters to maintain the acquired knowledge from prior tasks and only optimizing the newly added parameters to adapt to the new task."},
{"existing_parameters": "The existing parameters refer to the set of components or variables that have been previously learned and are currently in use within a system or model."},
{"existing_parameters__are__locked": "The predicate \"are\" indicates a state of being or condition, specifically that the existing parameters have a certain status or attribute."},
{"locked": "The object \"locked\" describes the condition of the existing parameters, meaning they are fixed and not subject to change or update during the learning process of new tasks."},
{"expanded_parameters": "The expanded parameters refer to the additional set of parameters introduced when a new task is encountered in a machine learning model. These parameters are distinct from the existing ones, which are typically frozen to preserve previously acquired knowledge."},
{"expanded_parameters__are__optimized": "The predicate \"are\" signifies the state or condition of the expanded parameters within the machine learning model. It indicates that these parameters are subject to a specific process or treatment as part of the model's learning strategy."},
{"optimized": "The object \"optimized\" describes the process applied to the expanded parameters. Optimization in this context means that these parameters are adjusted through a learning algorithm to improve the model's performance on the new task, while the existing parameters remain unchanged."},
