{"our_approach__introduces__more_learnable_parameters_compared_to_dualprompt": "The predicate \"introduces\" signifies that our approach brings about or incorporates a specific feature or characteristic into the model. In this context, it means that our approach adds a certain element to the model that was not present in the DualPrompt method."},
{"more_learnable_parameters_compared_to_dualprompt": "More learnable parameters compared to DualPrompt indicates that our approach includes a greater number of parameters that the model can adjust during training. This is in contrast to DualPrompt, which uses a specific configuration of prompt lengths and components. The increase in learnable parameters suggests a potential for greater flexibility and adaptability in the model."},
{"we__include_a_variant_of_out_method__coda_p_s": "The predicate \"include a variant of out method\" indicates that the authors have developed and are incorporating a modified version of their original method into the study. This variant is designed to be comparable to DualPrompt in terms of the number of parameters used."},
{"coda_p_s": "CODA-P-S is a variant of the CODA-P method designed to use a comparable number of parameters as DualPrompt, allowing for a fair comparison. It maintains the core principles of the original CODA-P approach but adjusts the parameter count to match that of DualPrompt. CODA-P-S is used in specific tasks and is often included in tables comparing various methods based on their performance metrics.|Here is another description: CODA-P-S is a method or algorithm evaluated in a comparative study alongside other techniques like ER, FT, LwF.MC, and L2P++. It is assessed based on specific metrics.|Here is another description: CODA-P-S is a specific method or algorithm within a comparative analysis, likely related to machine learning or data processing techniques. It is evaluated alongside other methods for its performance metrics.|Here is another description: CODA-P-S is a method or algorithm used in a specific context, likely related to performance metrics or evaluations. It is compared alongside other methods in terms of its effectiveness or output values."},
{"coda_p_s__uses__a_smaller_number_of_parameters_equal_to_dualprompt_for_additional_comparison": "The predicate \"uses\" in this context signifies the employment of a specific configuration or set of parameters by CODA-P-S to ensure a balanced comparison with DualPrompt. It indicates a deliberate choice in the design of CODA-P-S to align its parameter usage with that of DualPrompt."},
{"a_smaller_number_of_parameters_equal_to_dualprompt_for_additional_comparison": "A smaller number of parameters equal to DualPrompt refers to the configuration where CODA-P-S is adjusted to use the same quantity of learnable parameters as DualPrompt. This setup allows for a direct and fair comparison between the two methods, ensuring that any performance differences are not due to disparities in parameter count."},
{"our_method__outperforms__other_methods_even_under_this_condition": "The predicate \"outperforms\" indicates that the subject method is superior in performance compared to other methods. This superiority is measured under specific conditions, such as when the number of parameters is equal to that of DualPrompt."},
