{"a_dual_distribution_shift_benchmark": "A dual-distribution shift benchmark is a type of evaluation metric used in machine learning to test the robustness of models against two types of distribution shifts: semantic shifts and covariate shifts. Semantic shifts occur when the meaning of the data changes, while covariate shifts happen when the statistical properties of the input data change."},
