{"incremental_learning_with_self_organizing_maps": "'Incremental learning with self-organizing maps' is a research paper or publication that discusses the application of incremental learning techniques to self-organizing maps, a type of artificial neural network. The paper was presented at the 2017 12th International Workshop on Self-Organizing Maps and Learning Vector Quantization, Clustering and Data Visualization (WSOM).|Here is another description: Incremental learning with self-organizing maps is a research topic that explores the application of self-organizing maps (SOMs) in scenarios where data is continuously updated or expanded. This approach aims to adapt the SOM structure dynamically to accommodate new information without requiring a complete retraining of the model.|Here is another description: Incremental learning with self-organizing maps refers to a research paper or presentation by Alexander Gepperth and Cem Karaoguz, focusing on the application of self-organizing maps in incremental learning processes."},
