{"2017": "The year 2017 was pivotal in machine learning and neural networks, marked by several significant events and publications. Key highlights include the 12th International Workshop on Self-Organizing Maps, the introduction of the dual memory network for continual learning, and the publication of \"Overcoming catastrophic forgetting in neural networks.\" Notable contributions also came from the IEEE Transactions on Pattern Analysis and Machine Intelligence, the arXiv preprint arXiv:1705.03550, and the presentation of Gradient episodic memory for continual learning by David Lopez-Paz and Marc\u2019Aurelio Ranzato. Additionally, iCaRL was introduced at the IEEE Conference on Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition, and Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 30 was published, showcasing the state of research in neural information processing. The year also saw the influential paper \"Attention is all you need,\" introducing the Transformer architecture, which has become fundamental in advanced language models.|Here is another description: The year 2017 marks the specific edition of the International Conference on Machine Learning where various groundbreaking research papers, including the one by Friedemann Zenke, Ben Poole, and Surya Ganguli, were presented and discussed."},
