{"gradient_episodic_memory_for_continual_learning": "\"Gradient episodic memory for continual learning\" is a research paper by David Lopez-Paz and Marc\u2019Aurelio Ranzato, presented at the 31st International Conference on Neural Information Processing Systems in 2017. The paper introduces a novel approach to continual learning in neural networks, focusing on the use of gradient-based episodic memory to improve their ability to learn from a stream of data without forgetting previously acquired knowledge. This method aims to enhance the model's performance over time by retaining knowledge from previous tasks while adapting to new ones, mimicking human-like learning processes."},
