{"a_pre_trained_vision_encoder": "A pre-trained vision encoder is a machine learning model that has been previously trained to convert visual data into a format that can be understood and processed by other parts of the learning system, enhancing its ability to classify objects incrementally."},
{"\u03c6n": "\u03c6n refers to a specific parameter within the context of a continual learning model. It is part of a sequence of tasks designed to incrementally learn new object classes while maintaining performance on previously learned ones."},
{"\u03c6n__is_denoted_as__a_parameter": "\"is denoted as\" signifies the act of assigning a specific symbol or term to represent a concept or parameter within a mathematical or technical context. In this case, it is used to clarify the representation of \u03c6n."},
