{"paper__deals_with__class_incremental_continual_learning_setting": "The phrase \"deals with\" indicates that the paper addresses, discusses, or investigates the specified topic, which in this case is the class-incremental continual learning setting."},
{"class_incremental_continual_learning_setting": "The class-incremental continual learning setting is a scenario within continual learning where the model is required to learn new classes incrementally without forgetting the previously learned classes, and it operates without task labels during inference.|Here is another description: The class-incremental continual learning setting is a framework where a model is trained incrementally on new classes over time, without forgetting previously learned information. This setting is crucial for simulating real-world scenarios where data is continuously evolving."},
{"class_incremental_continual_learning": "Class-incremental continual learning is a specific type of continual learning where the model is required to learn new classes incrementally without forgetting previously learned classes. It involves updating the model as new classes are introduced over time."},
{"class_incremental_continual_learning__is__challenging": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the nature or characteristic of class-incremental continual learning, indicating that it possesses a certain quality or attribute."},
