{"motivation": "The motivation refers to the driving force or reason behind the experiments that include both class-incremental and domain-incremental continual learning. It is the underlying purpose that guides the research and experimentation in this field.|Here is another description: The motivation refers to the driving force or rationale behind the evaluation on the challenging _dual-shift_ benchmark using the ImageNet-R dataset. It is the underlying reason for conducting the experiments and analyzing the results."},
