{"continual_learning_more_practical": "Continual learning more practical refers to the objective of enhancing the applicability and effectiveness of continual learning techniques in real-world scenarios. This involves addressing challenges such as class and domain shifts to ensure that the learning system can adapt and perform well under varying conditions."},
{"our_work__does_not_change__technical_foundations_of_prompting": "The phrase \"does not change\" indicates that the current work maintains the existing methodologies or principles without alteration, specifically in regard to the technical aspects of prompting."},
{"technical_foundations_of_prompting": "The technical foundations of prompting refer to the established methods and principles used in the prompting process within the context of vision transformer encoders, as previously defined by the state-of-the-art DualPrompt approach.|Here is another description: The technical foundations of prompting refer to the underlying principles and methodologies used in the process of prompting within a specific context or application. In this case, it pertains to the prompting techniques employed in the field of vision transformers."},
{"technical_foundations_of_prompting__are_from__prior_state_of_the_art_dualprompt_65": "The phrase \"are from\" indicates the origin or source of the technical foundations of prompting. It suggests that these foundations are derived or based on a specific prior work or methodology."},
{"prior_state_of_the_art_dualprompt_65": "The prior state-of-the-art DualPrompt [65] is a previously established and highly regarded method or system for prompting in the context of vision transformers. It represents the cutting-edge approach in this domain at the time of its publication."},
