{"d__is__the_embedding_dimension_768": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the assignment or definition of a value to a variable or parameter within a model's architecture. It establishes the relationship between the parameter _D_ and its specific value, which is critical for the model's configuration and functionality."},
{"the_embedding_dimension_768": "The embedding dimension (768) refers to the size of the vector space used to represent embeddings in the model. An embedding dimension of 768 means that each word or token is represented as a 768-dimensional vector, allowing the model to capture complex relationships and nuances in the data."},
{"msa_layer": "The MSA layer, or Multi-head Self-Attention layer, is a component in transformer models that processes input data by attending to different parts of the input sequence simultaneously through multiple attention heads."},
{"msa_layer__has__input_h_r_l_d": "The predicate \"has\" in this context signifies that the MSA layer is characterized by or includes a specific input format or data structure necessary for its operation."},
{"input_h_r_l_d": "The input _**h**_ \u2208 R [L][\u00d7][D] represents a tensor where _L_ is the sequence length, _D_ is the embedding dimension (768 in this case), and _**h**_ is the input vector to the MSA layer, encapsulating the information from the input sequence in a high-dimensional space."},
