{"mitigating_catastrophic_forgetting__requires__avoidance_of_overwriting_knowledge_acquired_in_prior_tasks": "Requires indicates a necessary condition or action that must be taken to achieve a specific goal. In the context of mitigating catastrophic forgetting, it signifies that certain measures or strategies are essential to prevent the overwriting of previously acquired knowledge."},
{"avoidance_of_overwriting_knowledge_acquired_in_prior_tasks": "Avoidance of overwriting knowledge acquired in prior tasks means implementing methods to ensure that new learning does not erase or significantly alter the information from previous tasks. This can involve techniques such as freezing certain parameters, expanding the model, or optimizing only new components."},
{"new_task": "The new task refers to a subsequent learning task in a sequence of tasks designed to mitigate catastrophic forgetting in machine learning models. It represents the latest challenge or dataset that the model is being trained on after having learned from previous tasks."},
{"new_task__involves__freezing_current_components_and_expanding_the_set": "The predicate \"involves\" indicates the necessary actions or steps that are part of handling the new task. In this context, it describes the specific strategy employed when transitioning to a new task to preserve previously acquired knowledge."},
{"freezing_current_components_and_expanding_the_set": "Freezing current components and expanding the set is a strategy used to prevent the overwriting of knowledge from prior tasks. It involves locking the existing parameters of the model and only optimizing the parameters of the newly added components, thus allowing the model to learn from the new task without losing information from previous tasks."},
