{"expanding_the_capacity__of__a_nonlinear_model_like_an_mlp_module_transformer_attention_head_13_or_hypernetwork_63": "The phrase \"of a nonlinear model\" specifies the type of model to which the capacity expansion is being applied. It indicates that the model in question has nonlinear characteristics, meaning its output is not a linear combination of its inputs, which allows it to capture more complex relationships."},
{"a_nonlinear_model_like_an_mlp_module_transformer_attention_head_13_or_hypernetwork_63": "A nonlinear model like an MLP module, transformer attention head, or hypernetwork represents advanced machine learning architectures. An MLP (Multi-Layer Perceptron) module is a type of neural network with multiple layers that can model complex nonlinear relationships. A transformer attention head is part of the transformer architecture used in natural language processing, allowing the model to focus on different parts of the input sequence. A hypernetwork is a neural network that generates the weights for another neural network, enabling more dynamic and adaptive learning."},
