{"validation_data": "Validation data refers to a subset of the dataset used to tune model hyperparameters and make design decisions during the model development process. It is distinct from the training data used to teach the model and the test data used to evaluate its final performance.|Here is another description: Validation data in the context of the 5-task ImageNet-R benchmark refers to a set of images and corresponding labels that are not used during the training phase of model development. This data is essential for evaluating the model's ability to generalize its learning to new, unseen examples, providing an unbiased assessment of its performance and helping to fine-tune model parameters for optimal results."},
