{"evaluation_metrics__evaluate_methods_using__1_average_final_accuracy_an_or_the_final_accuracy_with_respect_to_all_past_classes_averaged_over_n_tasks_and_2_average_forgetting_fn_or_the_drop_in_task_performance_averaged_over_n_tasks": "The predicate \"evaluate methods using\" indicates the process of assessing or judging the effectiveness or quality of methods based on specific criteria or metrics. In this context, it involves using defined metrics to measure how well methods perform in retaining information across tasks."},
{"1_average_final_accuracy_an_or_the_final_accuracy_with_respect_to_all_past_classes_averaged_over_n_tasks_and_2_average_forgetting_fn_or_the_drop_in_task_performance_averaged_over_n_tasks": "The objects of evaluation are (1) average final accuracy AN, which measures the overall accuracy across all past classes averaged over N tasks, reflecting both the method's ability to learn new information and retain old information, and (2) average forgetting FN, which quantifies the decrease in task performance over N tasks, offering insight into the method's memory retention capabilities."},
