{"an": "AN refers to the average final accuracy, which is a critical metric used to evaluate the performance of methods in a series of tasks. It represents the final accuracy with respect to all past classes, averaged over N tasks.|Here is another description: _AN_ is a metric or method used in the context of evaluating performance across multiple tasks in a machine learning experiment. It is specifically applied in the ImageNet-R dataset scenario where tasks vary in the number of classes they contain.|Here is another description: _AN_ is a metric or method used in the evaluation of performance on the CIFAR-100 and DomainNet datasets. It is part of a comparative analysis that involves multiple trials to assess the effectiveness of certain approaches.|Here is another description: AN refers to a metric or method used in the context of evaluating performance across multiple tasks, specifically in the presence of domain shifts in the ImageNet-R dataset.|Here is another description: _AN_ is a metric or method used in the context of evaluating performance across multiple tasks in a machine learning experiment, specifically on the 10-task ImageNet-R dataset."},
{"an__is__the_more_important_metric_and_encompasses_both_method_plasticity_and_forgetting": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies that AN is being identified or defined as the more significant metric. It establishes the relationship between AN and its role in evaluating method performance."},
{"the_more_important_metric_and_encompasses_both_method_plasticity_and_forgetting": "The more important metric and encompasses both method plasticity and forgetting refers to AN's role as a comprehensive evaluation metric. It highlights that AN not only measures the final accuracy across tasks but also inherently accounts for both the adaptability (plasticity) of the method and the degree of forgetting observed during the learning process."},
{"fn": "FN, or average forgetting, is a metric used to evaluate the drop in task performance averaged over N tasks in the context of machine learning evaluations.|Here is another description: _FN_ is a metric used in the context of evaluating performance on the ImageNet-R dataset, specifically in relation to the average forgetting across multiple tasks.|Here is another description: _FN_ is a metric or method used in the context of evaluating performance on datasets like CIFAR-100 and DomainNet. It is specifically associated with measuring a certain aspect of model behavior over multiple trials.|Here is another description: FN is a metric used in the context of evaluating machine learning models, specifically in scenarios involving domain shifts and continual learning. It represents a measure that quantifies the performance of a model in retaining knowledge across different tasks or domains.|Here is another description: _FN_ is a metric used in the context of evaluating performance on a series of tasks, specifically in the ablation results on 10-task ImageNet-R. It is part of a comparative analysis where multiple trials are conducted."},
