{"arbitrary_size": "\"Arbitrary size\" refers to the unlimited or unrestricted capacity of the prompt pool in L2P, meaning it can be expanded to any size necessary without predefined limits, enabling it to adapt to various scenarios and demands."},
{"l2p_method": "The L2P method is a technique used in the context of prompt-based learning, where the performance is analyzed based on the size of the prompt pool. It is compared against other methods like DualPrompt in terms of average accuracy and upper bound performance.|Here is another description: The L2P method is a technique that involves using a prompt pool which can be scaled to an arbitrary size, aiming to improve performance in tasks by leveraging prompt components."},
{"l2p_method__peaks_with_a_pool_size_equal_to__twice_the_task_sequence_length": "The phrase \"peaks with a pool size equal to\" describes the optimal condition under which the L2P method achieves its highest performance. It indicates that there is a specific pool size at which the method performs best before its effectiveness begins to decline."},
{"twice_the_task_sequence_length": "\"Twice the task sequence length\" refers to the optimal size of the prompt pool for the L2P method, which is double the length of the task sequence. At this size, the L2P method reaches its peak performance, after which its effectiveness decreases."},
{"l2p_method__drops_in__performance": "The phrase \"drops in\" indicates a decrease or decline. In this context, it describes the reduction in effectiveness or efficiency of the L2P method when the size of the prompt pool exceeds a certain threshold, specifically twice the task sequence length."},
{"performance": "Performance in this context refers to the effectiveness or efficiency of the L2P method in accomplishing its intended tasks. It is measured in terms of accuracy and other relevant metrics, and it is observed to decrease when the prompt pool size is increased beyond a certain point."},
{"prompt_components__benefit_from__scale": "The phrase \"benefit from\" indicates that the _prompt_ _components_ experience a positive effect or improvement when a certain condition or factor is applied. In this context, it suggests that the performance of the _prompt_ _components_ is enhanced under specific circumstances."},
{"scale": "\"Scale\" in this context refers to the size or extent to which the _prompt_ _components_ can be increased or expanded. It implies that the performance of the _prompt_ _components_ improves as they are scaled up, meaning that larger or more extensive use of these components leads to better results.|Here is another description: \"Scale\" in this context refers to the size or extent of the prompt pool. It implies that as the size of the existing prompt pool is increased, the performance of the system using it begins to decline."},
