{"memory_aware_synapses_learning_what_not_to_forget": "\"Memory aware synapses: Learning what (not) to forget\" is a research paper co-authored by Marcus Rohrbach and Tinne Tuytelaars. The paper, presented at the European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) in 2018, explores methods for improving machine learning models by enabling them to selectively retain or discard information, mimicking the way human memory works.|Here is another description: \"Memory aware synapses: Learning what (not) to forget\" is a research paper presented at the European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV) in 2018, which discusses methods for improving machine learning models by making them more memory-aware, thus enhancing their ability to retain important information while learning new data.|Here is another description: Memory aware synapses: Learning what (not) to forget is a research paper authored by Marcus Rohrbach and Tinne Tuytelaars that introduces a novel approach to improve the performance of neural networks by selectively retaining important information and forgetting less relevant data.|Here is another description: \"Memory aware synapses: Learning what (not) to forget\" is a research paper authored by Marcus Rohrbach and Tinne Tuytelaars. The paper focuses on developing a method to improve machine learning models' ability to retain important information while learning new tasks, addressing the challenge of catastrophic forgetting."},
{"tinne_tuytelaars__authors__memory_aware_synapses_learning_what_not_to_forget": "The predicate \"authors\" indicates that Tinne Tuytelaars, along with Marcus Rohrbach, has written and is responsible for the content of the paper titled \"Memory aware synapses: Learning what (not) to forget.\""},
