{"2018": "The year 2018 was significant for several key publications and conferences in the field of machine learning and computer vision. Notable events included the publication of research papers on memory-aware synapses, end-to-end incremental learning, and lifelong learning techniques at the European Conference on Computer Vision (ECCV). Additionally, the IEEE International Conference on Big Data and the International Conference on Learning Representations (ICLR) took place, reflecting the state of research and technology in big data and learning representations. The AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence also featured a paper on measuring catastrophic forgetting in neural networks.|Here is another description: The year 2018 marks the specific edition of the Neural Information Processing Systems Workshop where the paper on theoretical insights into memorization in GANs was presented, highlighting the timeliness and relevance of the research within that year's conference.|Here is another description: The object \"2018\" specifies the year in which the arXiv preprint with the identifier arXiv:1809.10635 was published. This year marks the moment when the research on feedback connections for continual learning was disseminated for review and further development by other researchers."},
