{"online_continual_learning_with_maximal_interfered_retrieval": "\"Online continual learning with maximal interfered retrieval\" is the title of a research paper authored by the group of researchers, which was presented at the Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems conference in 2019. The paper discusses a method in machine learning that allows a model to continually learn from a stream of data while minimizing interference from previously learned information.|Here is another description: Online continual learning with maximal interfered retrieval is a research method or approach in the field of machine learning, specifically focusing on continual learning where a model learns sequentially from a stream of data without forgetting previously learned information. This technique emphasizes maximizing interference during the retrieval process to improve learning efficiency and adaptability."},
